@txc2768651338/dsh-effort-slider README · dsh-effort-slider：> 🔧 **v0.5.2** — Update the DSH development baseline to **0.2.1-rc.5** and validate packed releases on **rc.4 / rc.5**. Fix the stale npm 0.5.1 client artifact that still registered `dsh-effort-slider`, causing duplicate factory registration and a desktop startup reload loop. Packing now rebuilds the client and checks the actual JavaScript registration against the manifest, so a stale unscoped bundle cannot ship again. Mouse dragging now survives catalog refreshes triggered by live effort writes; requests are serialized with only the latest pending level retained, and the current model is checked again before saving.
>
> 🔧 **v0.5.1** — DSH **0.2.1-rc.2** compatibility: volatile settings with live updates, revision-checked provisioning, resolved `RemoteResult` failures, nested model-label slots, menu focus/blur integration, and safe handling of unavailable models and Session changes. The source build configuration uses the scoped package name; the stale npm artifact is corrected in v0.5.2. Live provisioning queues settings writes outside the active HMR transaction; CSS names and source maps stay stable across checkout paths

@txc2768651338/dsh-effort-slider README · Universal effort provisioning (v0.2.0, simplified in v0.3.0)：- **Wire-level provisioning (host, pi-ai)**: for `llm-pi-ai` models missing `reasoningEfforts`, the dictionary and `compat` wire dialect
  are patched in (**hot-applied, no restart**); pi-ai translates the level into real wire fields
  (`reasoning_effort` / `thinking` / OpenRouter `reasoning.effort`, etc.) **and** advertises the same declaration as the model's
  `reasoning` catalog metadata — which is what makes the official **Effort** row appear for a hand-declared model at all;
- **Client fallback scale**: if the directory returns no reasoning metadata, the panel still opens with the universal 5-level scale;
- Existing user declarations (`reasoningEfforts: false` or a custom dictionary) are always respected and never overwritten.

@txc2768651338/dsh-effort-slider README · Universal effort provisioning (v0.2.0, simplified in v0.3.0)：Supported wire dialects for custom endpoints (set `effort-slider.defaultDialect` or `routes.<route>`). A dialect translates
levels on `api: openai-completions` routes only — native protocols use pi-ai's built-in mapping, so the dialect setting
has no wire effect there:

@txc2768651338/dsh-effort-slider README · How It Works：> The browser half follows the official external-plugin convention: classic script + `window.__ModuleLoader__.load` factory;
> `react` / `react-dom/client` / `react/jsx-runtime` are platform externals;
> `effort.module.css` is hashed and inlined by lightningcss, injected as `<style data-plugin>` when the factory runs.

